 "narrative": "**SCALECRAFT SOCIAL SNAPSHOT — @talon__wilson**\n\n**WHERE YOU STAND**  \nYour overall score is 71. The biggest gaps come from a missing bio link/call‑to‑action (Profile Clarity 25) and posting less often than the target (Posting Consistency 61). What’s already working is that reels—especially those you post on Thursdays—drive more than three times the average engagement of your other content.\n\n**THE SINGLE BIGGEST OPPORTUNITY**  \nAdd a clear, clickable link and a concise CTA in your bio to turn the strong Thursday‑reel traffic into brand‑deal inquiries. Your reels average 668 engagements (3.5 × the account average) and the best Thursday reel hit 46.65 ×, so directing that audience to a media‑kit landing page can convert high‑interest viewers into sponsors.\n\n**YOUR 30‑60‑90 DAY PATH**  \n\n1. **Days 1–30 – Profile Upgrade:** Add a Linktree (or simple landing page) link to your bio and rewrite the first line to read “Adventure photographer & storyteller – open to brand partnerships.” This gives the 1,701 followers a place to click after seeing a high‑engagement reel and signals you’re ready for collaborations.  \n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + your weeks 1‑4 posting calendar  \n\n2. **Days 31–60 – Consistent Archive Posting:** Choose three fixed posting days—Thursday, Tuesday, Saturday—and schedule one reel for each using existing footage (e.g., the “Cape Flattery” clip, other travel B‑roll). Keep each prep under 30 minutes (voice‑over + text overlay). Posting on your strongest day (Thursday) lifts the cadence score and repeats the format that already outperforms the account.  \n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + your weeks 5‑8 posting calendar  \n\n3. **Days 61–90 – Brand‑Ready Reel Funnel:** For every reel you publish, open the caption with a hook and a CTA such as “Check the link in bio for my brand‑collab kit,” and add a brief on‑screen text prompt pointing to the bio link. Pairing the proven reel format with a direct next step channels the 13.46 % engagement rate into concrete sponsor leads.  \n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + your weeks 9‑12 posting calendar  \n\n**WHAT YOUR BEST POSTS HAVE IN COMMON**  \nThe top post is the “Cape Flattery” reel (Sep 17), a Thursday reel that earned 46.65 × the average engagement. Your three best posts are all reels, showcase striking outdoor scenery, were published on Thursdays, and open with a hook that teases the location (“The last few steps…”). The three lowest‑performing posts are also reels, posted on Tuesdays or Wednesdays, and begin with generic statements that lack an immediate hook.\n\n**WHAT THE FULL PLAN ADDS**  \nThe locked moves fill out the rest of each phase, give you a week‑by‑week posting calendar, and provide content prompts that repurpose your existing reels, carousels and behind‑the‑camera footage.",
